# AI-Driven CPU Scheduling Simulator with ML & RL

A reproducible, fully-tested CPU scheduling simulator developed for Operating Systems (AI3002). Features classical scheduling algorithms (FCFS, SJF, Round Robin, SRTF), a supervised Decision Tree policy recommender, and a tabular Reinforcement Learning (Q-learning) scheduler, accompanied by a FastAPI backend and React dashboard.

## Features

- **Unified Unit-Step Simulation Engine:** Discrete tick-level simulation supporting idle jumps, accurate context switch costs, and unified metric collection across all policies.
- **Classical Policies:** First-Come First-Served (FCFS), Shortest Job First (SJF), Shortest Remaining Time First (SRTF), and Round Robin (RR).
- **ML Policy Recommender:** Decision Tree model analyzing workload distribution features (load ratio, burst coefficient of variation, arrival patterns) to select the optimal scheduling algorithm under composite objectives.
- **RL Dynamic Scheduler:** Tabular Q-learning agent with a compact, permutation-invariant aggregate state space and rule-based action dispatch.
- **Scientific Evaluation:** Rigid seed separation (train, validation, test), empirical learning curves, regret analysis, and Jain's fairness index.
- **Web Dashboard:** Interactive FastAPI backend and modern React dashboard with Gantt chart visualization and real-time comparison.

## Project Structure

```
scheduling_simulator_rl/
├── config.py                 # Central configuration and hyperparameters
├── cli.py                    # Command-line interface
├── pyproject.toml            # Project dependencies and build configuration
├── src/schedsim/             # Core package
│   ├── domain/               # Process, Engine, Metrics, Timeline
│   ├── policies/             # FCFS, SJF, SRTF, RR, Registry
│   ├── workloads/            # Scenarios, Generator, Presets, IO
│   ├── ml/                   # Features, Labeling, Dataset, Decision Tree
│   ├── rl/                   # States, Actions, Gym-like Env, Q-Learning Agent
│   ├── evaluation/           # Experiment runner, Stats, Plots
│   └── api/                  # FastAPI routes and schemas
├── tests/                    # Comprehensive unit and integration test suite
├── data/                     # Workload files and datasets (generated)
├── models/                   # Saved ML & RL models
├── results/                  # Evaluation metrics, figures, and plots
├── docs/                     # Implementation progress, decisions, report notes
└── memory-bank/              # Multi-agent persistent memory bank
```

## Setup & Quickstart

1. **Activate Virtual Environment:**
   ```powershell
   .\.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
   ```

2. **Install Dependencies:**
   ```powershell
   pip install -e ".[dev]"
   ```

3. **Run Tests:**
   ```powershell
   pytest -q
   ```

4. **CLI Help:**
   ```powershell
   python cli.py --help
   ```
